      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is injected **into the environment of the spawned child process** \u2014 specifically, it is injected into the environment immediately before the child process starts.\n\nThe key points are:\n\n1. **Where it\u0027s injected**: Into the environment variables of the spawned Ingest agent child process (and the same applies to the Query agent).\n\n2. **When it\u0027s injected**: Immediately before the child process starts.\n\n3. **Where it is NOT**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated \u2014 the key is never held in the Hub\u0027s own environment.\n\n4. **How it gets there**: A local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and performs the injection.\n\nThis design ensures that a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only within the short-lived child process that actually makes the API calls.",
